<main data-lys>
<article id=\"answer\" aria-label=\"Overall barrier and turnaround evidence\">
  <div class=\"topline\"><div class=\"kicker\">Home retrofit · intake evidence</div><div class=\"index\">Program leads / 01</div></div>
  <header><h1>Which barrier leads overall—and did turnaround improve?</h1><p class=\"dek\">Current reports point to installer waits, but they cannot settle either cross-partner ranking or change over time.</p></header>
  <section class=\"answer\" aria-label=\"Answers\">
    <div class=\"answer-card primary\"><div class=\"label\">Most common barrier overall</div><div><strong>Cannot determine across partners</strong><p>North’s survey leader is installer scheduling; South’s case mentions are not a compatible measure.</p></div></div>
    <div class=\"answer-card caution\"><div class=\"label\">Did service turnaround improve?</div><div><strong>Not established</strong><p>8 days is a recent partial median; “around two weeks last spring” is an unmethoded note.</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class=\"sources\" aria-label=\"What each partner reported\">
    <section class=\"source north\" aria-labelledby=\"north-title\">
      <div class=\"source-head\"><h2 id=\"north-title\">Partner North</h2><span class=\"unit\">Survey · 40 homeowners</span></div>
      <div class=\"statline\"><span class=\"big\">28/40</span><div class=\"statcopy\"><b>Installer scheduling</b><br>70% selected</div></div>
      <p class=\"note\">Other selections: upfront cost 17/40; unclear eligibility 9/40. Multiple selections allowed, so counts overlap.</p>
      <span class=\"tag\">Within North: top reported barrier</span>
      <p class=\"note\">No service-turnaround times included.</p>
    </section>
    <section class=\"source south\" aria-labelledby=\"south-title\">
      <div class=\"source-head\"><h2 id=\"south-title\">Partner South</h2><span class=\"unit\">15 open cases reviewed</span></div>
      <div class=\"statline\"><span class=\"big\">9/15</span><div class=\"statcopy\">Cases mentioning<br><b>“waiting for an installer”</b></div></div>
      <p class=\"note\">Cases do not represent a reported total of homeowners served; other barriers were not recorded.</p>
      <div class=\"statline\"><span class=\"big\">8 days</span><div class=\"statcopy\">Median turnaround<br>for <b>11 of 15 cases</b></div></div>
      <p class=\"note\">4 cases had no time recorded. “Around two weeks last spring” has no identified cases, sample size, or method.</p>
    </section>
  </section>
  <aside class=\"need\"><h2>To answer both parts:<br>make the measures comparable</h2><p><strong>Barrier:</strong> shared period and coding; same denominator (e.g., homeowners or cases), complete capture, and a rule for multiple barriers. <strong>Trend:</strong> turnaround definition and method, sample size and missingness, plus a baseline collected on the same basis.</p></aside>
  <div class=\"footer\"><span>Source: separate partner summaries · recent intake period</span><span>Do not pool or infer change from these reports</span></div>
</article>
</main>
